! ============================================================
! 04c  Is your SCF solution actually a minimum?
! ============================================================
! H2 with the bond stretched to 2.5 A -- well past the point
! where example 05a showed the RHF curve going wrong.  Here we
! ask WHY, and get a quantitative answer instead of a graph.
!
! A converged SCF has found a STATIONARY point of the energy
! with respect to orbital rotations.  Nothing in the DIIS
! procedure checks that it is a MINIMUM.  A stability analysis
! computes the second derivative -- the orbital Hessian -- and
! reports its lowest eigenvalue in each of four channels.
!
! WHAT TO LOOK AT.  The four Seeger-Pople channels:
!
!   singlet (A+B)  real internal      +0.406  stable
!   singlet (A-B)  complex internal   +0.058  stable
!   triplet (A+B)  real EXTERNAL      -0.323  UNSTABLE
!   triplet (A-B)  complex external   +0.058  stable
!
! "Internal" means: is there a lower RESTRICTED solution?  No.
! Within the closed-shell manifold this really is a minimum,
! which is why the SCF converged happily and gave no warning.
!
! "External" means: is there a lower UNRESTRICTED solution?
! Yes, by a wide margin.  This is the triplet instability of
! stretched RHF, and it is the same physics as the Coulson-
! Fischer point in 05a, now expressed as a negative curvature
! rather than as a wrongly shaped curve.
!
! Note that the program REPORTS the external instability but
! does not follow it: descending that direction means changing
! the spin treatment of the whole calculation, which is a
! decision for you, not for the optimizer.  Act on it by
! adding %spin unrestricted and re-running.
!
! WHEN TO USE THIS IN PRACTICE.  Any of:
!   * a stretched or breaking bond,
!   * a diradical, a transition-metal centre, a charge-transfer
!     state,
!   * an energy that moves when you change %level_shift or the
!     initial guess,
!   * a TDDFT run that returns a NEGATIVE excitation energy --
!     that is the response equations finding the descent
!     direction the SCF missed.
!
! The cost is comparable to one TDDFT calculation.
%method  HF
%basis   6-31G
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%stability check

%geo
 H   0.0  0.0  0.0
 H   0.0  0.0  2.5
